API-29: initialise a new link's diameter, flow, status and setting

EN_addlink sets the diameter of a new pipe or valve but not of a new
pump, and never sets the new link's entries in the solver's flow,
status and setting arrays. Those arrays grow with realloc and keep the
values of a link deleted from the same slot, so a pump made with
EN_setlinktype reports another link's diameter, and a new link reads
another link's flow, status and setting until the next run (and the
stale flow becomes its starting flow). Set a pump's diameter to 0, as
the parser does, and start every new link with no flow at its initial
status and setting.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-29_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..23007d1 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -3491,6 +3491,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addlink(EN_Project p, const char *id, int linkType,
         link->Kc = 1.0; // Speed factor
         link->Km = 0.0; // Horsepower
         link->Len = 0.0;
+        link->Diam = 0.0;
     }
     else if (linkType <= PIPE)  // pipe or cvpipe
     {
@@ -3520,6 +3521,13 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addlink(EN_Project p, const char *id, int linkType,
     link->LeakArea = 0;
     link->LeakExpan = 0;
     link->InitSetting = link->Kc;
+
+    // A new link has no results yet: no flow, and its initial status
+    // and setting
+    hyd->LinkFlow[n] = 0.0;
+    hyd->LinkStatus[n] = link->InitStatus;
+    hyd->LinkSetting[n] = link->InitSetting;
+
     link->R = 0;
     link->Rc = 0;
     link->Rpt = 0;
